From 922fe86f24beb619bdf59acd7940a23c5d8ea535 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Castelló <bfcastello@gmail.com>
Date: Fri,  5 Jun 2026 00:38:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] scripts/entitlement: make Rez/SetFile non-fatal on
 macOS 12+

Rez and SetFile are Carbon-era developer tools that were removed from
Xcode Command Line Tools starting with macOS 12 (Monterey). When QEMU
is built on macOS 14+ CI runners (or modern developer machines), the
script exits under `set -e` before the final `mv` fires, so the signed
binary is never produced even though the build itself succeeded.

Make both calls non-fatal with `|| true`. The icon embedding step is
cosmetic and must not block binary delivery.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Castelló <bfcastello@gmail.com>
---
 scripts/entitlement.sh | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/entitlement.sh b/scripts/entitlement.sh
index 0f412949ec..a31618c14d 100755
--- a/scripts/entitlement.sh
+++ b/scripts/entitlement.sh
@@ -25,9 +25,9 @@ if test -n "$ENTITLEMENT"; then
   codesign --entitlements "$ENTITLEMENT" --force -s - "$SRC"
 fi

-# Add the QEMU icon to the binary on Mac OS
-Rez -append "$ICON" -o "$SRC"
-SetFile -a C "$SRC"
+# Add the QEMU icon to the binary on Mac OS (Rez/SetFile absent in CI is non-fatal)
+Rez -append "$ICON" -o "$SRC" || true
+SetFile -a C "$SRC" || true

 mv -f "$SRC" "$DST"
 trap '' exit
--
2.49.0
